title HUNK65 — tap the filter strip
prompt Keep going Lindy-first crux-first on the Season A Photos journey; approve own design rounds; send each finished increment.
think HUNK64 painted the filter strip a keeper reads, yet reading is not choosing — the selection still moved by a discrete call. The crux: a finger on the glass. This is the exact parallel of HUNK55 tapping the history filmstrip.
think Transplanted HUNK55's pixel-to-band idiom verbatim: band_px = tcols·skate.cell_w, tap_band(x) = x/band_px, null off the strip (x<0 or band>=count). tap_at selects that filter via HUNK63 select_to, and paint is HUNK64 paint_strip unchanged — so the band tapped is the band marked, no drift, the same no-drift discipline HUNK55 carries.
think A tapped filter then commits into the shared history via HUNK63 commit — proven by tapping noir (band 3, two verbs) and asserting the committed view equals apply_preset noir byte-for-byte.
obs Built and ran GREEN on the first try; the tap idiom is now proven three times over (HUNK50 edits, HUNK55 filmstrip, HUNK65 filter strip). Cleaned an inline @import into a top-level const.
obs brushstroke/ already on the TAME roster; tame_style_scan_bans GREEN, width exit 0.
